WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.467
Retrieval pipeline design.

2
00:00:02.767 --> 00:00:06.114
Everything so far snaps together into one architecture.

3
00:00:06.114 --> 00:00:06.967
Let's draw it.

4
00:00:08.167 --> 00:00:09.700
Here is the whole pipeline.

5
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.967
Offline, we parse the documents.

6
00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:13.200
We chunk them.

7
00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.467
We embed the chunks and index them in a vector store.

8
00:00:16.767 --> 00:00:18.900
Online, we first rewrite the query.

9
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:23.267
Then retrieve with hybrid search, and rerank before assembling the prompt.

10
00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:27.067
Mature pipelines pull ahead on the query side.

11
00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:33.600
Query rewriting turns a conversational follow-up into a standalone search query, using chat history.

12
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:39.300
Multi-query generates three paraphrases, retrieves for all, and unions the results.

13
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:44.300
And HyDE has the LLM write a hypothetical answer, and embeds that.

14
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:46.967
Why does HyDE work?

15
00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:52.033
A question sits in one region of vector space, and the real document in another.

16
00:00:52.333 --> 00:00:56.773
But a hypothetical answer, even an invented one, looks like a document.

17
00:00:56.773 --> 00:00:59.400
So it lands much nearer to the real thing.

18
00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.000
Here they are, composed.

19
00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:06.367
Rewrite the question, then make paraphrases and a hypothetical answer.

20
00:01:06.667 --> 00:01:09.633
Retrieve for each of them and union the candidates.

21
00:01:09.933 --> 00:01:12.833
Finally rerank against the real, rewritten query.

22
00:01:14.033 --> 00:01:20.200
A user asks what caused the Artemis three comms dropout, then follows with: and how long did it last?

23
00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:24.300
No chunk resembles that sentence, so retrieval returns nothing.

24
00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:29.067
Rewriting turns it into: duration of the Artemis three comms dropout.

25
00:01:29.367 --> 00:01:34.433
On the eval, a third of which were follow-ups, that alone lifts hit-rate fourteen points.

26
00:01:35.633 --> 00:01:36.495
Let's recap.

27
00:01:36.495 --> 00:01:39.367
Ingest means parse, chunk, embed, index.

28
00:01:39.667 --> 00:01:42.700
Query means rewrite, retrieve, rerank, assemble.

29
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:46.333
Rewriting, multi-query, and HyDE boost recall.

30
00:01:46.633 --> 00:01:49.311
And every arrow is a dial you can measure.

31
00:01:49.311 --> 00:01:50.267
Next up: FAISS.
